From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GK <5311779+kruteev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:40:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add optional start and stop sounds for Dictation (#1690)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* Add optional start and stop sounds for Dictation

A Play sounds toggle in Dictation › Commands, off by default. The system Pop
plays on the microphone's first samples, half a second later for a Bluetooth
microphone whose headset is still switching profile, and ducking starts with
it. Stopping restores the volume at once and plays Pop again before the
microphone closes. Cancelling is silent.

* Play synthesized start and stop chimes for Dictation

Start rises a fourth and stop falls back down it, so the two read apart
without looking. Scripts/gen-dictation-sounds.js synthesizes both WAVs,
so no third-party audio ships and every run writes the same bytes.

* Turn Dictation sounds on by default

---------

Co-authored-by: abue-ammar <iabueammar@gmail.com>
